/**
 * C1: THE SCHOOL FROM THE INSIDE (docs/43-lessons.md §15.3, part 4).
 *
 * Late winter of the family's third year (`docs/reviews/c1-cast.md`). Mark is
 * seven and halfway through his first school year, and he has started
 * correcting his parents' Estonian with the words his teacher uses: "Isa, see
 * on ju omastav!" So the part opens on the morning show's segment about
 * homework, and on the grammar words an Estonian school names things with
 * (`nimisõna`, `alus`, `öeldis`, the cases by their Estonian names), which are
 * the words a learner needs for what this part explains once in the level: a
 * long sentence and a long text that hold together, the comma before every
 * subordinate clause and the signposts (`cohesion`, lesson 20). Then the
 * school's messages, the class trip to the museum where Anna sees Mark
 * sitting on his own, the evening Mark says nobody plays with him at break,
 * the morning show's guest on children who are left out, the formal letter to
 * the head of the school (the part's one `write`, 200 words), and the meeting
 * with Piret and Toomas, where the move is disagreeing with somebody in
 * authority, politely and firmly (§15.5). The storyline is gentle and ends
 * well: Mark is asked what he wants, the school does something, and a week
 * later he is playing football at break.
 *
 * Who is who is `docs/reviews/c1-cast.md`. Mark speaks in no lesson, as in
 * B2: what he says is passed on by his parents, and he is in a lesson's cast
 * only so his name may be used. Kaire, the parent from B2's parents' evening
 * (`b2-pere.ts`, lesson 18), is the mother of Grete, a girl in Mark's class,
 * and speaks in lesson 22. The museum guide in lesson 21 is a role name
 * (`Giid`). Oskar and Hugo, the two boys of Mark's class, and Grete, are
 * named and never heard.
 *
 * In preview (`preview.ts`) until C1 is the course, and held to every check a
 * lesson is (`npx tsx scripts/check-lesson-part.ts --part c1-kool`).
 */

